# Ygra against Oko, Thief of Crowns' +1 ("loses all abilities and becomes a green Elk creature with base power and toughness
# 3/3"), which has the later timestamp both times.
# Mox Jet, no creature: Oko's type-setting effect makes it one, which changes what Ygra's "Other creatures are Food
# artifacts" applies to, so Ygra's effect depends on it and applies after it (CR 613.8a): a Food artifact Elk creature.
# In layer 6 neither depends on the other (applying "loses all abilities" doesn't change that it is a creature), so they
# go in timestamp order (CR 613.7) and Oko's, the later, takes Ygra's "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this permanent: You gain 3 life"
# with the rest: the refusal, with the mana for it floating.
# Elvish Mystic, a creature already: Oko's effect changes nothing about what Ygra's applies to, so neither depends on the
# other and timestamp order has Oko's "becomes a creature" replace the artifact type and Food that Ygra's effect added
# (CR 613.1d, 205.1a): only an Elk creature. Before Oko it is a Food artifact Elf Druid.

